SD-patch 0010: consolidated JiuwenSwarm startup-latency patch (formerly
seven separately numbered patches; consolidated so one patch owns each
file region and repeated `swarm-patches.py apply` stays idempotent).

Root cause (measured on the dist50 cold install, 2026-10-25 16:02 run):
AgentServer schedules its nonblocking warmups right after listen, but
ensure_persistent_checkpointer() executes heavy synchronous sections on
the event loop (~9.5s on a cold install tree: module imports plus
sqlite creation). While the loop is blocked the server cannot accept
or handshake new WebSocket connections, so the Gateway's connect
attempt waits idle and its connection.ack only lands after
"persistent checkpointer ready" (observed: handshake handled at
43.906, checkpointer ready at 43.893, ack at 43.910). The same
coupling exists on the warm repo tree at ~4s scale. On top of that,
the import chain ahead of listen paid for modules the first request
did not need: the feishu SDK (~4.7s, imported even with the channel
disabled), the heartbeat chain (~2.8s), the heavy tui_connect module
(~1.8s), and the AgentServer import pulling pandas/pdfplumber/milvus
(~6.8s), plus a channel-config settle window (0.75s -> 0.2s) ahead of
the homepage RPC batch.

Changes (one patch, one file region each):
- gateway/app_gateway.py: feishu SDK lazy-import guard; tui_connect
  preload in a worker thread during the agent-server connect retry;
  channel-config settle window 0.75s -> 0.2s; IM pipelines built on a
  worker thread after the preload resolves; socket imported at module
  top so the probe loop performs no function-level imports.
- agents/swarm/context.py, common/utils.py,
  server/runtime/agent_manager.py, server/runtime/agent_adapter/interface.py,
  server/agent_ws_server.py: heartbeat import chain deferred off the
  critical path.
- agents/harness/common/tools/__init__.py, gateway/__init__.py,
  gateway/cron/__init__.py, server/app_agentserver.py,
  server/runtime/agent_manager.py, server/agent_ws_server.py:
  AgentServer import slimming - pandas/pdfplumber/milvus stay out of
  the import path until actually used.
- server/agent_ws_server.py + gateway/routing/agent_client.py: the
  Gateway<->AgentServer connect path no longer waits on warmups; the
  ws handshake performs no imports.
- server/agent_ws_server.py: every post-listen warmup (checkpointer,
  mcp prewarm, personal context, image modality) gated behind the
  first Gateway connection, with their module imports preloaded in
  worker threads, so the listen -> first-handshake window is free of
  background warmup work.

Effect: the listen -> first-handshake window is free of every
background warmup's imports and sync sections, so the Gateway connects
and receives connection.ack immediately after the port opens.
Measured on the Windows desktop line (same-machine A/B on gateway
startup stage logs): warm restart ~17.5s -> ~5-7s; user-perceived cold
start 50s+ -> 20-25s.

Known leftover (documented for follow-up): after the first ack the
checkpointer warmup still blocks the AgentServer loop for its duration
on cold trees - first requests during that window queue. Fully fixing
that requires moving the synchronous sections of
ensure_persistent_checkpointer off the event loop, which touches
openjiuwen upstream behaviour and is deferred.

